    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YWjtKsLbFBfV3ynQseWxLE)_\n\nStacked on #147 (base is its branch; retarget to main once #147 merges).\n\n## What\nTwo new faces, `sp-text-face` (Org and other text modes) and `sp-minibuffer-face` (minibuffer and posframe), are added to `fontaine-faces`. Presets set `:sp-text-face-height` and `:sp-minibuffer-face-height`: 1.36 in the `t` fallback (what 4 `text-scale` steps of 1.08 came to) and 1.0 in `presentation`, whose `default` height is already 220.\n- `sp-text-buffer` and `sp-minibuffer` now map those faces onto `default` with `face-remap-add-relative` instead of `text-scale-increase`. `sp-fonts-text-scale-steps` (#146) is removed. `text-scale` (`s-=`, `s--`) still works on top.\n- `sp-posframe--set-text-size` still drops inherited remappings first, then maps `sp-minibuffer-face`.\n- The plain minibuffer is now also at Org size (1.36); before it was two steps (about 1.17).\n- Docs and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). Assumed, not checked: a float `:height` in a remapped `default` spec multiplies the base `default` height. `fontaine-faces` is a `defconst` in fontaine 3.1.0 and is extended with `add-to-list`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9cVX4xhp367pqb88n)_",
